From f401f8d3223bd5bd3d756c3b3c3b62ff18ca39bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xkazm04 <kazdan@seznam.cz>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 10:24:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 08/35] feat(art): skinned player hands with sleeves and
 regional skin under the non-flat looks

apps/vr/art/hands/build_hands.py builds both forearms and hands from an MPFB (MakeHuman CC0)
adult male with the game_engine rig (three bones per finger and thumb), a dark wool sleeve over
each forearm, and a regional skin albedo (tanner backs, pinker palms and tips, redder
knuckles, nails from MPFB's mask) plus ORM (AO, roughness, skin mask) in a UV of their own.
-run=CreatePlayerHands imports SK_PlayerHands into /Game/Look/Shared/Hands with
M_PlayerHandsEpic (subsurface skin), M_PlayerHandsLite (default lit, the quest fallback) and
M_PlayerSleeve. Look/PlayerHandsLook poses the bones from the 26-joint HandFrame by aiming
each bone at its child joint with the palm normal kept, so no rotation convention enters.
UHandPresentationComponent draws it instead of the mannequin when the look is not flat (flat
unchanged); in the S1 shot only, a one-handed pose gets its mirror so both hands show, as S1.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
