From feed45662d6f5a18824cdc017ab46e4dd371ff16 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xkazm04 <kazdan@seznam.cz>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 10:37:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 12/35] feat(art): painted cheering crowd under the non-flat
 looks

Two studio stills (GPT Image 2.5, 2 of Tier B's 40) of colourful Roman spectators on chroma
green, keyed and packed by apps/vr/art/crowd-painted/pack_crowd.py into T_CrowdPainted: five
painted figures per T57 crowd variant at that variant's own card aspect, colours dilated under
the alpha. -run=CreateCrowdPainted builds M_CrowdPainted in /Game/Look/Shared/Crowd (masked,
lit, a little self-light; the T57 custom data unchanged, flat banners stay flat).
CrowdLook::Apply re-points each card's atlas rect at a painted figure of its variant and swaps
the material under any non-flat look, so cards keep size, place and orientation; flat keeps
the clay crowd and its tint tests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
