From 2c8332ceb8777817678e999f3b536d248e43859d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xkazm04 <kazdan@seznam.cz>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 10:57:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 17/35] fix(art): straight player thumbs and warm tanned hand
 skin

The recorded clips curl the thumb into a hook (the ward clip's distal phalanx bends about 130
degrees back on the one before it), which the skinned thumb drew as a pale claw. For the
picture only, PlayerHandsLook now holds each thumb segment within 30 degrees of the one
before it, lengths kept; the gesture pipeline never sees it. The regional skin is rebaked
warm and tanned (darker backs, pinker knuckles and tips, S1), and one tan multiply
(SkinTint 0.86, 0.72, 0.60; -MageArenaHandTint= overrides) is applied in Create for both
non-flat looks, so quest and epic hands match.

