From: xkazm04 <kazdan@seznam.cz>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 11:14:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 20/35] feat(look): capture-s1 -Mobile, the S1 shot on the
 mobile renderer proxy

-Mobile renders the S1 shot at the ES3.1 feature level (mobile forward
shaders on desktop D3D12, headless with -RenderOffScreen), with
AndroidEngine.ini's cvars and the Meta_Quest_3 device profile's scalability
(Android_Mid: post, texture, effects, AA 1; OpenXR: shadow 2). MobileHDR stays
the project's (not set anywhere, so the engine default, on); -MobileLdr turns
it off, Meta's usual Quest setting. A cold run compiles the mobile shader
cache in about 3 minutes on Lynx.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 apps/vr/tools/capture-s1.ps1 | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/apps/vr/tools/capture-s1.ps1 b/apps/vr/tools/capture-s1.ps1
index 7c469fa..0405afc 100644
--- a/apps/vr/tools/capture-s1.ps1
+++ b/apps/vr/tools/capture-s1.ps1
@@ -10,6 +10,11 @@ param(
 	[ValidateSet("flat", "quest", "epic")][string]$Look = "flat",
 	[string]$Out = "",
 	[double]$RivalM = 0,
+	# The mobile renderer proxy: the ES3.1 feature level (mobile forward shaders on desktop D3D12), the project's
+	# Android cvars (AndroidEngine.ini) and the Meta_Quest_3 device profile's scalability (Android_Mid with shadow 2).
+	[switch]$Mobile,
+	# With -Mobile: MobileHDR off (Meta's usual Quest setting: no post pass at all), not the project default (on).
+	[switch]$MobileLdr,
 	[string]$ExtraArgs = "",
 	[int]$TimeoutMinutes = 15
 )
