diff --git a/docs/research/QUEST-LOOK-2026-10-28.md b/docs/research/QUEST-LOOK-2026-10-28.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9c75dc2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/research/QUEST-LOOK-2026-10-28.md
@@ -0,0 +1,115 @@
+# Quest look: the record (graphics push, 2026-10-28)
+
+Tier A of `docs/concepts/GRAPHICS-PUSH-2026-10-28.md`: can the build that ships on Quest 3 look like key art S1? Branch
+`push/quest-look`, behind `-MageArenaLook=quest` (flat stays byte for byte the greybox; the suite holds 345/348 every
+round, the three reds being the known Lynx-only `Fire.Golden`, `Overlay.Golden`, `Rivals.NullPath`). Blind judges:
+baseline 14.0, quest r3 26.3, quest r7 24.0 (epic r6 27.0). r8 answers round 2's notes; not yet judged.
+
+## 1. What it is, file by file
+
+All under `apps/vr/Game/Source/MageArenaVR/` unless a path says otherwise.
+
+**The yardstick (shared)**
+- `Look/S1ShotCapture.*` and `apps/vr/tools/capture-s1.ps1`: `-MageArenaS1Shot` freezes the Brennic semifinal, poses
+  Brennic (bout-start distance, 16.2 m; Cast clip paused), one Fire bolt 3.2 m out, the ward raised through the hand
+  pipeline, camera pitch -10. Writes `s1-game.png` (layout FOV) and `s1-keyart.png` (Brennic at half the frame height).
+  From the settle on it holds the animation clocks at 12.5 s (world game time for material `Time`, and
+  `QuestSpells::Clock` for the presentation's flipbooks): two runs differ by 0.11/255. `-Mobile [-MobileLdr]` is the mobile
+  renderer proxy (section 3). `-RivalM` is an exploration shot.
+
+**Quest look (quest only)**
+- `Look/QuestLook.*`: everything the arena builder asks for under the quest look. Surfaces (one material instance each),
+  lights (sun, captured sky light, haze, four pylon point lights, exposure compensation without MobileHDR), the painted
+  sky dome, dressing (wall and pole banners, dais ledge, four pylons with fire bowls), fire cards (two licking flame
+  cards and a halo per fire, posed once to the fixed seat), Brennic's and the hands' quest materials (a 0.5 s scan
+  applies them when the meshes appear), the camera grade (filmic, fixed exposure, modest bloom; no colour grade in post).
+- `Look/CreateQuestLookAssetsCommandlet.*` (`apps/vr/tools/look/create-quest-look-assets.ps1`): builds `/Game/Look/Quest`
+  headless. `M_Q_Surface` (world-aligned mapping: tops in X/Y, sides along the face; normal map turned into world space
+  along the same axes; contact darkening at wall bases and the sand's rim; macro variation), `MI_Q_*` per surface,
+  `M_Q_Sky` (panorama on the view direction, mirrored at +/-90 degrees), `M_Q_Banner`, `M_Q_Brennic` (Tier B's textures,
+  default lit, skin wrap, gold rim), `M_Q_Hands` (Tier B's textures, tan tint 0.74/0.60/0.50, wrap, roughness 0.5).
+- Small branches in `Greybox/ArenaGreyboxActor.cpp` (material per surface, shadow casters, lights/sky/dressing),
+  `Greybox/ArenaStands.cpp` (crowd tint gain x3), `Hands/MageArenaPawn.cpp` (camera).
+
+**Shared with the epic look (every look but flat)**
+- `Look/QuestSpells.*` and `Look/CreateQuestSpellAssetsCommandlet.*` (`apps/vr/tools/look/create-quest-spell-assets.ps1`):
+  `M_Q_SpellGlow` (replaces `M_SpellGlow`, same T63 cells, painted fireball/water shells, HDR heart for warm colours
+  only), `M_Q_BoltCore` (swirling flame core in the threat colour, ragged masked rim; a black core stays black),
+  `M_Q_Ward` (two wave stills panning on 18 upright cards round the palm, lifted in the shader along the arch curve),
+  `M_Q_EnvFire` (painted licking flame, additive), `M_Q_SpellHalo` (soft additive glow: the glow Quest has without bloom).
+  Hooks: `Session/SpellVfx.cpp` (glow material), `Session/SessionPresentation.cpp` (bolt core, trail, halo, white-gold
+  heart, Brennic's cast fire and halos, ward spray within 1.7 m, Brennic 1.1x and his HP bar, carved Wardstones with a
+  rune-flame cap), `Greybox/HandPresentationComponent.cpp` (ward cards).
+- `Look/RivalBackdrop.*`: the dark gate in the far wall behind Brennic.
+- `Budget/BudgetStressPlan.cpp` (the census plans the new core material), `Budget/BudgetStressDriver.cpp` (counts the
+  skinned hands).
+
+**Textures** (studio GPT Image 2.5 stills, 11 of 40 used; prompts in
+`C:/Users/kazda/mage-art-staging/push-1028/textures/prompts/*.txt`): sand, flagstone, sky (16:9), banner (9:16),
+fireball, water splash, ward wave x2 (16:9), tall flame (9:16); plus the orchestrator's stone blocks.
+`apps/vr/tools/look/prep_quest_textures.py` (tileable crops and cross-fades, normals from luma, sky haze and soft sun)
+writes `apps/vr/art/look/quest/`; `apps/vr/tools/look/prep_spell_textures.py` (the 2048 BC7 flipbook keeping the T63
+layout, the two-wave panorama, the flame, the core noise) writes `apps/vr/art/look/spells/`.
+`apps/vr/tools/look/grade_compare.py` measures four regions against S1.
+
+## 2. D-G4 per round (`capture-budget.ps1 -ExtraArgs "-MageArenaLook=quest"`; limits 150 draws, 350k BasePass tris)
+
+| Round | Draws median / p95 | BasePass tris | What moved it |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| r1 | 137 / 141 | 146k | Textured arena, shadowed sun (shadow-depth draws), sky dome replacing the panel stack |
+| r2 | 122 / 125 | 148k | Greybox flame spheres off under quest; flames became cards later |
+| r3 | 139 / 142 | 171k | Tier B's skinned hands (+29k tris, 2 base + 4 shadow draws), halos, rune layers, fire cards |
+| r4 | 141 / 145 | 171k | Painted crowd, ward arch, gate |
+| r5 | 144 / 148 | 171k | Hand halos, glow pool, spray layers |
+| r6 | 135 / 139 | 170k | Shadow casting off on hands, pylon bowls, dais ledge, wall cloth (-9 draws) |
+| r7 | 136 / 140 | 171k | Coping (instanced into the wall, +0), styled cuff |
+| r8 | 136 / 139 | 170k | Hot-heart layer (+1) |
+
+Frame time on Lynx (emulated x64, desktop forward) stays 7-8.5 ms median; it is not a Quest number.
+
+## 3. The mobile renderer
+
+`-FeatureLevelES31` runs headless on Lynx (D3D12 at ES3_1, shader platform PCD3D_ES3_1; a cold run compiles the mobile
+shaders in about 3 minutes). Reproduce:
+
+    powershell -NoProfile -File apps/vr/tools/capture-s1.ps1 -Look quest -Mobile [-MobileLdr] -Out runs/push/quest/<round>-mobile
+
+`-Mobile` adds AndroidEngine.ini's cvars (mobile forward, 2 CSM cascades at 1024) and the Meta_Quest_3 device profile's
+scalability (Android_Mid: post, texture, effects, AA 1; OpenXR: shadow 2). MobileHDR is set nowhere in the project, so
+the shipping build has the engine default, on.
+
+- **MobileHDR on:** mean difference from desktop forward 5/255. Tonemapper, bloom, CSM shadows, translucent cards, the
+  four point lights and every material hold.
+- **MobileHDR off** (`-MobileLdr`, Meta's usual Quest setting): no post pass, so no exposure bias, no filmic shoulder, no
+  bloom, no vignette. The frame read about 20 % brighter (sand value 0.93 against 0.79). Fixed by scaling sun, sky light
+  and point lights by 0.78 when the feature level is mobile and `r.MobileHDR` is 0 (`QuestLook.cpp`, `FQuestTuning`). The
+  additive halo cards stand in for bloom. Judges called the LDR frame "nearly the same image" as desktop.
+- **What the proxy cannot show:** ASTC compression (desktop uses BC), multiview, foveation, the real GPU frame time.
+
+## 4. Engine pitfalls met
+
+- A spawned directional light is static: set it Movable **before** `SetActorRotation`, or it stays level along +X (the flat
+  look's sun has this; left alone so flat stays byte-identical).
+- Virtual shadow maps under forward shading drew no shadows: the quest look sets `r.Shadow.Virtual.Enable 0` (Quest uses
+  CSM anyway).
+- HLSL custom nodes: `lit` and `tan` are intrinsics; naming a variable either fails the material silently (grey checker).
+  A grayscale sampler on a TC_Default texture fails too.
+- `-run=CreateCuffStyled` cannot re-save its assets once they exist (it loads them and does not delete first); the
+  committed assets were used.
+- The engine's unlit debug material cannot be instanced: use a plain mesh component (the gate).
+- Heredoc tooling turned `\\n` into real newlines in generated HLSL; write edit scripts to files.
+
+## 5. The grade lesson
+
+Region statistics against S1 (`grade_compare.py`) steered the sky and the shade toward teal-lilac. Every number moved
+toward S1, and the blind judges called the result "a muddy mauve dome" and "cold and pinkish". S1 reads golden-peach to a
+viewer. r8 restored the warm panorama and warm shade. Measure, but let a viewer's read of the whole frame decide.
+
+## 6. Open items, ranked
+
+1. Hand skin a touch too orange and saturated on the mobile LDR frame.
+2. Faint vertical seams between the ward cards.
+3. The GPU p95 spike in r8's D-G4 run (25.7 ms against ~3.8 ms before): likely contention with the other tier's Unreal
+   process, unverified.
+4. The wall still about 0.1 saturation high (0.58 against S1's 0.48).
+5. On a Quest 3: the ASTC look of the painted textures, and the real frame time with MobileHDR on and off.
-- 
2.56.0.windows.2


